// Locked into a Power Siphon: a program pinned in the wall to run the base.
// The power is the player's gain; this is the price the program keeps.
//
// A stretch memory written once per `SIPHON_GRUDGE_PERIOD` (1000 ticks), so
// it builds over a long hold. At the cap it is -6 x 9 = -54: a Steady
// program sulks after two strikes (-12 crosses `MORALE_SULKS_AT`, -8) and
// downs tools at the cap (-54 past `MORALE_DOWNS_TOOLS_AT`, -50); an
// Abrasive one reaches -75.6, just past lashing out. One strike alone (-6)
// does not sulk. It crosses the tantrum line on its own, which is why
// `tests/disposition.rs` exempts it by name beside `unslotted`: the hold is
// preventable, release it.
//
// Every strike while held resets the clock, so decay only sets the way back:
// from -54 to `MORALE_RECOVERED_AT` (-6) is log2(9) = 3.17 half-lives, about
// 7900 ticks at 2500. Slower than `unslotted` because this one is the
// player's deliberate price.
//
// `BaseTile`, `note_postings`' subject: the siphon's own tile.
(
    id: "siphoned",
    name: "Held in a Siphon",
    blurb: "Pinned in the wall and left to run the base.",
    valence: -6.0,
    half_life: 2500,
    subject: BaseTile,
    strike_cap: 9,
)
